From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] include: add the external shell opt-in check

Purpose: one definition of the switch that limits the external XP shell's
changes to the processes that ask for them.
Change: wine/win4wine.h provides win4wine_external_shell(), true when
WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL is in the environment (with any value). Unix
libraries read the Unix environment, PE modules the process environment,
as the individual checks did. The session sets it to 1 for the XP shell,
its helpers and the bridge proxy.
Scope: no behaviour by itself. Ordinary Wine applications do not set the
variable and keep Wine's behaviour in every later patch that uses it.
---
 include/wine/win4wine.h | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/wine/win4wine.h b/include/wine/win4wine.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..69eb777
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/wine/win4wine.h
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+/*
+ * Opt-in check for the external XP shell (win4wine)
+ *
+ * The changes made for the external XP shell apply only to processes that
+ * have WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL in their environment (with any value), so
+ * that ordinary Wine applications keep Wine's behaviour. Unix libraries
+ * read the Unix environment, PE modules the process environment.
+ */
+
+#ifndef __WINE_WINE_WIN4WINE_H
+#define __WINE_WINE_WIN4WINE_H
+
+#ifdef WINE_UNIX_LIB
+
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+static inline BOOL win4wine_external_shell(void)
+{
+    return getenv( "WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL" ) != NULL;
+}
+
+#else
+
+static inline BOOL win4wine_external_shell(void)
+{
+    return GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 ) != 0;
+}
+
+#endif
+
+#endif  /* __WINE_WINE_WIN4WINE_H */
